hospice chaplains&#x02019; experiences with patients requesting physician-assisted suicide. <source>J Palliat Med</source><year>2005</year>;<volume>8</volume>:<fpage>1160</fpage>-6.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16351529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Goy ER, Dobscha SK. Why Oregon patients request assisted death: family members&#x02019; views. <source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>2008</year>;<volume>23</volume>:<fpage>154</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18080719</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Passik SD, Dugan W, McDonald MV, Rosenfeld B, Theobald DE, Edgerton S. Oncologists&#x02019; recognition of depression in their patients with cancer. <source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1998</year>;<volume>16</volume>:<fpage>1594</fpage>-600.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9552071</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Simon GE, VonKorff M. Recognition, management, and outcomes of depression in primary care. <source>Arch Fam Med</source><year>1995</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>99</fpage>-105.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7842160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Perez-Stable EJ, Miranda J, Munoz RF, Ying YW. Depression in medical outpatients: underrecognition and misdiagnosis. <source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>1990</year>;<volume>150</volume>:<fpage>1083</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2184790</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="other">Compassion and Choices of Oregon. 2007. <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.compassionoforegon.org">www.compassionoforegon.org</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="ref22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="other">Appelbaum PS, Grisso T. <source>MacArthur competence assessment tool for clinical research (MacCAT-CR)</source> Sarasota,