page>861</fpage>-5.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4436473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Beck A, Brown G, Berchick R, Stewart B, Steer R. Relationship between hopelessness and ultimate suicide: a replication with psychiatric outpatients. <source>Am J Psychiatry</source><year>1990</year>;<volume>147</volume>:<fpage>190</fpage>-5.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2278535</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Minkoff K, Bergman E, Beck A, Beck R. Hopelessness, depression, and attempted suicide. <source>Am J Psychiatry</source><year>1973</year>;<volume>130</volume>:<fpage>455</fpage>-9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4691303</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="other">First MB, Spitzer RL, Gibbon M, Williams JBW. <source>User&#x02019;s guide for the structured clinical interview for DSM-IV axis I disorders: clinician version</source> New York: Biometrics Research Department, <year>1997</year></citation></ref><ref id="ref32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chochinov HM, Wilson KG, Enns M, Lander S. Prevalence of depression in the terminally ill: effects of diagnostic criteria and symptom threshold judgments. <source>Am J Psychiatry </source><year>1994</year>;<volume>151</volume>:<fpage>537</fpage>-40.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7511875</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref33"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Johnston WS, Hoffman WF. Correlates of suffering in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. <source>Neurology</source><year>1999</year>;<volume>52</volume>:<fpage>1434</fpage>-40.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10227631</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref34"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Nelson HD, Schmidt TA, Kraemer DF, Delorit MA, Lee MA. Physicians&#x02019; experiences with the Oregon Death with Dignity Act. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>342</volume>:<fpage>557</fpage>-63.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10684915</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref35"><label>35</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Fenn DS, Lee MA, Heintz RT, Bloom JD. Attitudes of Oregon psychiatrists toward physician-assisted suicide. <source>Am J Psychiatry </source><year>1996</year>;<volume>153</volume>:<fpage>1469</fpage>-75.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8890683</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref36"><label>36</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Leong GB, Fenn DS, Silva JA, Weinstock R. Evaluation of competence to consent to assisted suicide: views of forensic psychiatrists. <source>Am J Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>157</volume>:<fpage>595</fpage>-600.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10739419</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref37"><label>37</label><citation citation-type="journal">Tolle SW, Tilden VP, Drach LL, Fromme EK, Perrin NA, Hedberg K. Characteristics and proportion of dying Oregonians who personally consider physician-assisted suicide. <source>J Clin Ethics</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>111</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15481162</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref38"><label>38</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ganzini L, Beer TM, Brouns M, Mori M, Hsieh YC. Interest in physician-assisted suicide among Oregon cancer patients. <source>J Clin Ethics</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>17</volume>:<fpage>27</fpage>-38.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16689111</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p><bold>Cite this as: </bold><italic>BMJ</italic> 2008;337:a1682</p></notes></back></article>